Functional validation flow for KB creation, approval, discovery, editing, and Agent integration

1. Create KB & Trigger Pipeline Ingestion

Navigate: From the left sidebar, click Build ➔ Knowledge Base (or click Create on the top bar ➔ Knowledge Base).
Select Level: Choose your Hierarchy Level from the top dropdown (e.g., Organization / Team).
Fill Details: Enter KB Name & Description.
Upload Files: In the Source section, upload your test document(s).
Configure Pipeline: Click through the stepper steps (Cleanse ➔ Chunking ➔ Embedding ➔ Destination) using defaults.
Build Pipeline: On the Review step, click Create / Build Pipeline and wait for the progress bar to finish.
Send for Approval: Click the Send for Approval button in the top right header.

2. Approve Knowledge Base

Navigate: From the left sidebar / header, click Approvals (or switch to Console ➔ Approvals).
Locate Request: Under the Knowledge Base tab, find your newly submitted KB.
Approve: Click the Approve button on the item card or review popup.

3. Verify in Discovery

Navigate: From the left sidebar, click Discovery (or Marketplace).
Filter & Search: Select the Knowledge Bases tab and search for your KB name.
Preview: Click on the KB card to open it and verify the files and status are displayed in read-only view.

4. Edit KB & Re-submit for Approval

Navigate: In Discovery (or via Account / My Creations), locate your KB card.
Click Edit: Click the three dots (⋮) menu on the card and select Edit.
Modify: Add a new file or change the description/pipeline settings.
Save & Submit: Click Save Changes (to re-run ingestion) and then click Send for Approval.

5. Re-Approve & Verify Update

Navigate: Go back to Approvals from the main menu.
Approve Revision: Locate the updated KB and click Approve.
Verify: Go back to Discovery ➔ Knowledge Bases ➔ open your KB card to confirm the newly added file is present.

6. Create Agent & Attach the KB

Navigate: From the left sidebar, click Build ➔ Agent (or click Create ➔ Agent).
Match Level: Ensure the Hierarchy Level at the top matches the exact same level used for the KB.
Fill Details: Enter Agent Name and Instructions / Prompt.
Attach KB: In the Knowledge Base section/widget on the builder canvas, click Add Knowledge Base (+ button).
Select & Apply: Find your approved KB in the popup modal, select the checkbox, and click Apply / Add.
Save & Test: Click Save Agent, then click Playground / Test to test queries against the attached KB.

Overall Expected Flow

Create KB → Run Pipeline → Send for Approval → Approve → Verify in Discovery → Edit → Re-run Ingestion → Re-submit → Re-approve → Verify Update → Attach KB to Agent → Test in Playground.

